  "implemented_contracts": [
    "Typed owned Animation/Dispelling/Interruption, exact Common, distinct bound roles and exact registered requirement bits; deliberately finite14-operation/20-rule catalog. No source words or book acceptance grant host authority.",
    "Animation stages claim,10mana, fresh actor generation, owned plan/provenance and absolute lifetime together. Available/spent registered remains are distinct from actor health or fixture objects; failed admission leaves the claim/resources/actor world intact.",
    "Opaque reusable incarnation-bound servant commands check exact living owner and servant generations, then share one metered staged3dp/contact50 attack resolver with existing wards and Attack restrictions. Dismissal/removal/expiry cannot retarget a replacement or unspend remains.",
    "Opaque InfluenceRef binds domain/instance and actor/object generation to the current incarnation. Normal live prepare/release rechecks key+primitive/schema, permission, cost and current contribution; repeated/stale/default/foreign/wrong-kind inputs refuse. Dispel removes only one Disguise or Attack restriction, preserving injury/payments/truth/history/other effects.",
    "Owned Checkpoint retains actual servant/pending/attachment/influence plans, spent claims, owners, clocks and identities alongside prior items/events/perception. Whole proposed restore validates first, preserves destination on refusal and issues fresh incarnation; old command/influence/pending/ticket/event authority never revives.",
    "Independent connected M4 book/revision caller destroys authoring inputs and original host, restores combined servant/restriction/disguise/witness/rune/paid-annulus state, then demonstrates real command injury, perception change, one-charge healing, exact onset/slow/servant expiry and replacement safety.",
    "Optional exact pending interruption uses a distinct opaque incarnation/action/caster-generation input and normal paid spell, not administrative cancel. It removes only the named still-pending action, retains paid costs/completed history, owns the interrupted-action report, and cannot retarget reused queue slots. Checkpoint rewind is explicit."
  ],
